# How this blog publishes instantly

This post lives in a **content store**, not in the app source. The site fetches it,
renders it, and caches the result — so adding a post never triggers a rebuild.

{% callout type="tip" %}
Content posts are Markdoc: Markdown plus a few tags for embeds, callouts, figures, and code.
{% /callout %}

## Rich blocks

A YouTube embed:

{% youtube id="dQw4w9WgXcQ" title="Example video" /%}

A code block:

```ts
export async function getContentPost(slug: string) {
  const meta = await readJson(`posts/${slug}/metadata.json`);
  const markdoc = await readText(`posts/${slug}/article.mdoc`);
  return meta && markdoc ? { meta, markdoc } : null;
}
```

| block | tag |
|---|---|
| video | `youtube` |
| post | `x` |
| note | `callout` |
| image | `figure` |

## Why it works this way

{% callout type="info" %}
The app reads this file at request time and revalidates every minute, so a new post is
live without rebuilding the site.
{% /callout %}
